text = "[center][font_size=44][glow color=#ff8c26 radius=14][b]GlyphuxRichLabel[/b][/glow][/font_size][/center]
BBCode with [b]bold[/b] and [i]italics[/i] (the variable font's weight axis and a slant), [u]underline[/u], [s]strikethrough[/s], [color=#ffb347]colors[/color], [font_size=34]sizes[/font_size], [outline_size=2][outline_color=#5a1030][color=#ffc0d8]outlines[/color][/outline_color][/outline_size], [glow color=#40c0ff radius=10]glows[/glow] and [shadow color=#e04070 offset=3,3 blur=2]shadows[/shadow].

Animation runs in the shader: [wave amp=60 freq=6]waves[/wave], [shake rate=14 level=14]shaking[/shake] and [rainbow freq=1 sat=0.7 val=1 speed=0.4]rainbows of many colors[/rainbow] cost nothing on the CPU. Emoji come from the font's fallbacks: 🔥😀🤖. Lines wrap at the control's width, between words, and [url=https://github.com/Azazel-Labs/Glyphux]links[/url] report clicks with their meta.

